  "schema": 1,
  "name": "hairline_rays",
  "description": "hundreds of fine bright hairlines sweeping out of the spiral centres and crossing in a mesh, blue-white on deep blue",
  "reference": {
    "image": "sear-the-sky-25.jpg",
    "folder": "fractal-drive-sync/style-refs",
    "made_with": "Ultra Fractal orbit traps (signed exoteric.roach.org), 2560x1600"
  },
  "suggested_colormap": "hairline_rays",
  "reuses": [
    "the radial channel (a near-flat ground, the map's lower 0.6)",
    "de glows for the set's lace and bloom",
    "the tone pass"
  ],
  "adds": [],
  "notes": [
    "The stroke trap is item 062's primitive, for five references whose look is a clean continuous curve drawn like a pen stroke (visionary-spires, ten-leaf-clover, tinan, tianan, sear-the-sky). A line through the critical value (`on_c`) pulls back as stars joined by long curves, a circle as closed loops; the distance is taken in the frame, so a stroke keeps one weight along its whole pullback, which the strip trap's blades and a `de` glow do not. Three stacks came of it: mercury_tubes (lit tubes), neon_loops (glowing outlines; cream_ribbons and tan_star_beams are its palette entries) and hairline_rays (hairlines at `taper` 0).",
    "Three line strokes at `taper` 0 (tilts 20, 80 and 140 degrees), each a hairline of one width with a faint halo: at a spiral seat every step's pullback sweeps round the centre, and three lines' pullbacks cross as a mesh. The set itself is kept faint (the lace at 0.08), since the reference shows lines and nodes, not a set.",
    "Round one's lessons: with a bloom on the `de` channel the lace-heavy spiral seats drew the set and hid the lines; `smallest` 0.02 drops the short fur along the set that 0.004 draws. A deep seat costs minutes: the loop runs until the curves are frame-sized. Readings: r_one (one line), r_six (six: a dense mesh), r_taper (`taper` 0.25: the long lines thicker)."
  ],
